    "peer_reviewed": "Journal of Imaging",
    "problems": "Only five architectures were compared; the networks were pretrained and fine-tuned for 8 epochs, so the study does not test training from scratch or arbitrary-label fitting. Images were 2D slices, and the authors state that the method is not ready for clinical deployment. Results are repeated 10 times and bootstrapped, but the setup does not include a natural-label/random-label control.",
    "rows_left_out": "No reported train/test accuracy rows were left out. Other separately reported test metrics (BA, F1, F2, MCC, sensitivity and specificity) and bootstrap ranks/intervals are not included as separate rows because they do not test a mapped version; the text reports them in Tables 6–11.",
